From 55f65f573e1ae2a56d59de804a446fc3023e4151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:07:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Case + warranty claim assignment (ASCM)

Implements the still-to-build case assignment feature, plus the equivalent
for warranty claims (which needed a schema change first, since
ascm_warranty_claims had no assigned_to column).

Case assignment:
- CaseController::assign() -- validates assigned_to (nullable, must exist
  in users), updates the case, logs a CaseNote with entry_type:
  'assignment'.
- PATCH ascm/cases/{case}/assign route.
- AscmShellController now passes $assignableUsers (role=employee only,
  now that roles exist) to both the cases and warranty views.
- cases.blade.php: Assigned column + assign <select> in the off-canvas
  panel, prefilled with the row's current assignee and pointed at the
  right case's /assign URL.

Warranty claim assignment:
- Migration: assigned_to (nullable FK -> users.id) on
  ascm_warranty_claims, same shape as ascm_cases.assigned_to.
- Migration: adds 'assignment' to ascm_warranty_claim_notes.note_type
  enum (mirrors ascm_case_notes.entry_type, which already had it) --
  raw ALTER...MODIFY on MySQL / drop+recreate on SQLite, same pattern as
  the users.role refactor migration and for the same doctrine/dbal
  reason.
- WarrantyClaim::assignee() relation.
- WarrantyController::assign() + route + note-logging, same pattern as
  cases.
- warranty.blade.php: same Assigned column + assign <select> treatment.

Assignment sync between linked cases and claims (raised during review):
flagging a warranty issue through the mock e-commerce trigger
(HelpDeskMockController -> CaseController::store) already creates a case
and, when there's an eligible registration, a claim with case_id pointing
at it -- so a case and a claim can legitimately be the same piece of
work. To keep them from drifting apart:
- CaseController::assign() cascades the new assignee down to every
  warranty claim linked to that case (a case can have several -- see
  SupportCase::warrantyClaims, hasMany) and logs a synced 'assignment'
  note on each.
- WarrantyController::assign() cascades the new assignee up to the one
  case a claim is linked to, if any (case_id is nullable/singular), and
  logs a synced 'assignment' note on the case.

Not fixed (pre-existing, out of scope): WarrantyController::storeNote()
saves note_type: 'internal', which was never a valid
ascm_warranty_claim_notes.note_type value (decision/service_plan/general,
now +assignment). Flagging separately rather than folding into this
patch.
